-- title:
--   Existence of the Cartier dual p-divisible group
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $p,h$ be natural numbers (neither primality of $p$ nor positivity of $h$ is assumed). Let $G$ be a $p$-divisible group over $R$ of height $h$ in the sense of the structure [`PDivisibleGroup`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199), that is: a family of commutative rings `G.level v` for $v \in \mathbb{N}$, each carrying a cocommutative Hopf $R$-algebra structure and finite and free as an $R$-module; transition maps `G.transition v : G.level (v+1) →ₐc[R] G.level v`, each an algebra and coalgebra morphism over $R$ and surjective; the rank condition $\operatorname{finrank}_R(G.\mathrm{level}\ v) = p^{vh}$ for all $v$; and the identification of kernels $\ker(G.\mathrm{transition}\ v) =$ `torsionIdeal R (G.level (v+1)) (p^v)`, the ideal generated by the image of the augmentation ideal of `G.level (v+1)` under the algebra map induced by multiplication by $p^{v}$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a $p$-divisible group $G'$ over $R$ with the same parameters $p,h$ together with a Cartier duality datum between $G$ and $G'$ (the predicate `IsCartierDual` being the non-emptiness of the type `CartierDuality G G'`), i.e. isomorphisms of $R$-algebras-and-coalgebras $G'.\mathrm{level}\ v \cong$ [`CartierDual R (G.level v)`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDual.html#L12) for every $v$, compatible with the transitions in the sense that for all $v$, all $x \in G'.\mathrm{level}(v+1)$ and all $a \in G.\mathrm{level}(v+1)$, the functional attached to $G'.\mathrm{transition}\ v\, x$ evaluated at $G.\mathrm{transition}\ v\, a$ equals the functional attached to $x$ evaluated at the image of $a$ under multiplication by $p$.
--
--   This is the construction of the dual $p$-divisible group, of the same height, as in Tate's article on $p$-divisible groups: dualising the quotient maps induced by multiplication by $p$ yields the transitions of the dual tower. It is used in the project wherever the Tate module of a $p$-divisible group is paired with that of its dual, in particular in the analysis of Galois actions on Tate modules of Jacobians of modular curves at ordinary primes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_exists_isCartierDual.lean

